IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc17-dna-samples`

-- ccc17-tests-dna-samples.l4 -- tests for ccc17-dna-samples.l4 (ss 487.056 to 487.0911). Expected values are written from the text, beside each assertion.

§ `Tests: s 487.056 when and by whom`

-- (1): an order under 487.051(4) with a place, day and time -> paragraph (a); any other case -> paragraph (b)
#ASSERT `s 487.056(1) the time at which the samples shall be taken under section 487.051` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 487.056(1)(a) at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
#ASSERT `s 487.056(1) the time at which the samples shall be taken under section 487.051` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 487.056(1)(b) on the day on which the order authorizing the taking of the samples is made or as soon as feasible afterwards`
#ASSERT `s 487.056(1) the time at which the samples shall be taken under section 487.051` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)
#ASSERT `s 487.056(2) the time at which the samples shall be taken under section 487.055 or 487.091` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 487.056(2)(a) at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11) or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
#ASSERT `s 487.056(2) the time at which the samples shall be taken under section 487.055 or 487.091` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 487.056(2)(b) as soon as feasible after the authorization is granted`
#ASSERT `s 487.056(2) the time at which the samples shall be taken under section 487.055 or 487.091` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)
#ASSERT `s 487.056(3) the time at which the samples shall be taken when the person fails to appear` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 487.056(3)(a) when the person is arrested under a warrant issued under subsection 487.0551(1) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
#ASSERT `s 487.056(3) the time at which the samples shall be taken when the person fails to appear` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 487.056(3)(b) as soon as feasible after the person appears at the place set out in the order or summons`
#ASSERT `s 487.056(3) the time at which the samples shall be taken when the person fails to appear` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) to (6)
#ASSERT `s 487.056(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply even though the order or authorization is appealed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.056(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply even though the order or authorization is appealed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.056(5) the peace officer may cause the samples to be taken in the place` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.056(5) the peace officer may cause the samples to be taken in the place` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.056(5) the peace officer may cause the samples to be taken in the place` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.056(5) the peace officer may cause the samples to be taken in the place` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.056(6) the samples are taken by a person the subsection permits` `s 487.056(6) a peace officer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.056(6) the samples are taken by a person the subsection permits` `s 487.056(6) a person acting under the direction of a peace officer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.056(6) the samples are taken by a person the subsection permits` `s 487.056(6) someone else` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.056(6) the samples are taken by a person the subsection permits` `s 487.056(6) a peace officer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.056(6) the samples are taken by a person the subsection permits` `s 487.056(6) a peace officer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests: s 487.057 report, s 487.058 immunity`

#ASSERT `s 487.057(1) the peace officer shall make a written report in Form 5.07 and cause it to be filed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.057(1) the peace officer shall make a written report in Form 5.07 and cause it to be filed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.057(1) with whom the report shall be filed` `s 487.057(1) a warrant under section 487.05` EQUALS JUST `s 487.057(1)(a) with the provincial court judge who issued the warrant or granted the authorization, or another judge of that provincial court`
#ASSERT `s 487.057(1) with whom the report shall be filed` `s 487.057(1) an authorization under section 487.055` EQUALS JUST `s 487.057(1)(a) with the provincial court judge who issued the warrant or granted the authorization, or another judge of that provincial court`
#ASSERT `s 487.057(1) with whom the report shall be filed` `s 487.057(1) an authorization under section 487.091` EQUALS JUST `s 487.057(1)(a) with the provincial court judge who issued the warrant or granted the authorization, or another judge of that provincial court`
#ASSERT `s 487.057(1) with whom the report shall be filed` `s 487.057(1) an order under section 487.051` EQUALS JUST `s 487.057(1)(b) with the court that made the order under section 487.051`
#ASSERT `s 487.057(1) with whom the report shall be filed` `s 487.057(1) another instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.057(2) the report shall include the matter` `s 487.057(2)(a) a statement of the time and date the samples were taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.057(2) the report shall include the matter` `s 487.057(2)(b) a description of the bodily substances that were taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.057(2) the report shall include the matter` `s 487.057(2) another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.057(3) the peace officer shall send a copy of the report to the other peace officer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.057(3) the peace officer shall send a copy of the report to the other peace officer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.057(3) the peace officer shall send a copy of the report to the other peace officer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.058 the person incurs no criminal or civil liability for the thing done` `s 487.058 a peace officer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.058 the person incurs no criminal or civil liability for the thing done` `s 487.058 a person acting under a peace officer’s direction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.058 the person incurs no criminal or civil liability for the thing done` `s 487.058 someone else` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.058 the person incurs no criminal or civil liability for the thing done` `s 487.058 a peace officer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.058 the person incurs no criminal or civil liability for the thing done` `s 487.058 a peace officer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests: s 487.06 procedures, s 487.07 duty to inform, detention, privacy, young person`

#ASSERT `s 487.06(1) the means is one by which the peace officer is authorized to take samples of bodily substances` `s 487.06(1)(a) the plucking of individual hairs from the person, including the root sheath` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.06(1) the means is one by which the peace officer is authorized to take samples of bodily substances` `s 487.06(1)(b) the taking of buccal swabs by swabbing the lips, tongue and inside cheeks of the mouth to collect epithelial cells` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.06(1) the means is one by which the peace officer is authorized to take samples of bodily substances` `s 487.06(1)(c) the taking of blood by pricking the skin surface with a sterile lancet` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.06(1) the means is one by which the peace officer is authorized to take samples of bodily substances` `s 487.06(1) another means` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.06(1) the means is one by which the peace officer is authorized to take samples of bodily substances` `s 487.06(1)(c) the taking of blood by pricking the skin surface with a sterile lancet` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.06(2) the warrant, order or authorization shall include the term or condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.06(2) the warrant, order or authorization shall include the term or condition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.06(3) the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, may take fingerprints from the person for the purpose of the DNA Identification Act` `s 487.06(3) an order made under section 487.051` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.06(3) the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, may take fingerprints from the person for the purpose of the DNA Identification Act` `s 487.06(3) an authorization granted under section 487.055` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.06(3) the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, may take fingerprints from the person for the purpose of the DNA Identification Act` `s 487.06(3) an authorization granted under section 487.091` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.06(3) the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, may take fingerprints from the person for the purpose of the DNA Identification Act` `s 487.06(3) a warrant issued under section 487.05` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.06(3) the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, may take fingerprints from the person for the purpose of the DNA Identification Act` `s 487.06(3) another instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 487.07(1): paragraphs (a) to (d) always; (e)(i) only for a warrant; (e)(ii) only for a warrant and a young person
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(a) the contents of the warrant, order or authorization` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(b) the nature of the investigative procedures by means of which the samples are to be taken` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(c) the purpose of taking the samples` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(d) the authority of the peace officer and any other person under the direction of the peace officer to use as much force as is necessary for the purpose of taking the samples` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(e)(i) the possibility that the results of forensic DNA analysis may be used in evidence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(e)(i) the possibility that the results of forensic DNA analysis may be used in evidence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(e)(ii) the rights of the young person under subsection (4)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(e)(ii) the rights of the young person under subsection (4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(e)(ii) the rights of the young person under subsection (4)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` `s 487.07(1)(a) the contents of the warrant, order or authorization` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(2)(a) the person may be detained for the purpose of taking the samples` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(2)(a) the person may be detained for the purpose of taking the samples` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(2)(a) the person may be detained for the purpose of taking the samples` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(2)(b) the person may be required to accompany a peace officer for the purpose of taking the samples` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(2)(b) the person may be required to accompany a peace officer for the purpose of taking the samples` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(3) the taker shall ensure that the person’s privacy is respected in a manner that is reasonable in the circumstances` `s 487.07(3) a peace officer who takes samples of bodily substances from a person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(3) the taker shall ensure that the person’s privacy is respected in a manner that is reasonable in the circumstances` `s 487.07(3) a person who takes such samples under the direction of a peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(3) the taker shall ensure that the person’s privacy is respected in a manner that is reasonable in the circumstances` `s 487.07(3) someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(4) the young person has the right to consult counsel and an adult and to have the warrant executed in their presence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(4) the young person has the right to consult counsel and an adult and to have the warrant executed in their presence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(4) the adult with whom the young person may consult and in whose presence the warrant is to be executed` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 487.07(4) a parent`
#ASSERT `s 487.07(4) the adult with whom the young person may consult and in whose presence the warrant is to be executed` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 487.07(4) an adult relative`
#ASSERT `s 487.07(4) the adult with whom the young person may consult and in whose presence the warrant is to be executed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 487.07(4) any other appropriate adult chosen by the young person`
#ASSERT `s 487.07(4) the adult with whom the young person may consult and in whose presence the warrant is to be executed` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 487.07(5) the young person’s waiver of the rights under subsection (4) is valid` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(5) the young person’s waiver of the rights under subsection (4) is valid` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(5) the young person’s waiver of the rights under subsection (4) is valid` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 487.07(5) the young person’s waiver of the rights under subsection (4) is valid` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests: s 487.071 verification, s 487.08 use, offences`

